WEBVTT

00:02.470 --> 00:05.260
What do <i>you</i> suggest we do, then?

00:06.690 --> 00:09.070
But what I like about you

00:09.070 --> 00:12.480
is that you just speak your mind without 
thinking about the consequences.

01:44.050 --> 01:48.490
Number 16, Nara Prefecture, 
Shikagou High School.

01:48.950 --> 01:49.920
Bronze.

01:51.190 --> 01:55.790
Number 17, Wakayama 
Prefecture, Kaeichuu High School.

01:56.180 --> 01:57.130
Silver.

02:00.060 --> 02:04.580
Number 18, Kyoto Prefecture, 
Kitauji High School.

02:05.000 --> 02:06.390
Gold.

02:07.720 --> 02:09.170
We, did it!

02:10.040 --> 02:11.480
Not yet.

02:12.880 --> 02:15.170
We made it past the first hurdle.

02:15.170 --> 02:15.860
Yes.

02:16.590 --> 02:20.260
Moving on, I will now 
announce the three schools

02:20.260 --> 02:24.150
to be competing in the Nationals 
this coming October.

02:24.790 --> 02:31.870
First, Number Five, Osaka Prefecture, 
Myoujou Technical School.

02:34.130 --> 02:35.020
Second,

02:36.520 --> 02:41.620
Number Nine, Kyoto Prefecture, 
Ryusei Academy High School.

02:42.850 --> 02:43.880
Lastly,

02:46.600 --> 02:47.690
the third school...

02:53.280 --> 02:58.420
Number 18, Kyoto Prefecture, 
Kitauji High School.

02:56.400 --> 02:57.970
Yes!

03:07.080 --> 03:08.130
We did it.

03:08.130 --> 03:09.300
We're in the Nationals.

03:10.370 --> 03:14.290
<b>Episode 11</b>

03:10.370 --> 03:14.290
<b>Orchestra to the Future</b>

03:14.290 --> 03:16.550
Congratulations
 Concert Band
 National Concert
 Band Competition

03:14.290 --> 03:16.550
Congratulations
  Concert Band
 Kansai Concert Band
 Competition Gold

03:15.800 --> 03:19.660
I think your speech made a difference.

03:19.660 --> 03:20.500
I know.

03:20.500 --> 03:22.960
That really changed the mood.

03:23.670 --> 03:25.430
Good morning.

03:25.820 --> 03:27.310
Morning.

03:27.310 --> 03:28.850
Wow!

03:28.850 --> 03:30.430
It's the Nationals version!

03:30.430 --> 03:32.260
Looks awesome, huh?

03:32.260 --> 03:33.080
It does!

03:33.080 --> 03:37.410
Everyone was saying we might get 
gold in the Nationals this year.

03:38.070 --> 03:40.580
It really was amazing.

03:40.580 --> 03:42.620
Especially the trumpet and euph soli.

03:42.620 --> 03:45.820
Our other seniors were saying 
it gave them chills.

03:45.820 --> 03:47.190
K-Kaho!

03:48.540 --> 03:50.130
S-Sorry!

03:50.130 --> 03:52.560
Oh, no, it's totally fine.

03:52.560 --> 03:55.200
I'm going to do the best I can.

03:55.900 --> 03:59.040
I want you to graduate with the gold.

03:59.440 --> 04:00.680
Sally-chan...

04:02.100 --> 04:03.520
Let's do this.

04:03.520 --> 04:04.220
Yeah.

04:04.950 --> 04:06.260
Well, see you!

04:06.260 --> 04:07.800
See you after school.

04:09.080 --> 04:10.700
<i>I was flustered.</i>

04:11.180 --> 04:13.590
<i>Rather, I was in shock.</i>

04:14.750 --> 04:17.600
<i>That performance undoubtedly amazing.</i>

04:18.170 --> 04:22.560
<i>Mayu-chan was playing to 
Reina's sound perfectly.</i>

04:22.560 --> 04:24.300
<i>She was matching her.</i>

04:25.250 --> 04:29.600
<i>Did Taki-sensei know this would happen?</i>

04:30.120 --> 04:31.750
Kitauji for the win!

04:30.120 --> 04:31.750
Tarobei

04:30.120 --> 04:31.750
Can't argue against Kitauji's Nationals nomination
 That trumpet-euph soli was really good

04:30.120 --> 04:31.750
Jirutaya@2A

04:30.120 --> 04:31.750
Kitauji was insane

They're in their own league.

04:30.410 --> 04:33.030
Someone wrote about it here, too.

04:33.030 --> 04:36.230
They're talking about how good 
the euph and trumpet soli was.

04:36.230 --> 04:37.730
I saw one, too.

04:38.160 --> 04:41.270
They were saying it might be even better 
than the miracle performance a couple years ago.

04:41.270 --> 04:43.390
Oh, Kumiko-senpai.

04:43.390 --> 04:44.760
Hello again.

04:44.760 --> 04:46.430
Hey.

04:46.430 --> 04:47.250
Come on.

04:47.250 --> 04:49.630
Less talk, more practice.

04:49.630 --> 04:50.830
Okay.

04:51.550 --> 04:54.100
Well, shall we get started, too?

04:54.100 --> 04:55.190
Kumiko-chan.

04:55.970 --> 04:57.270
Thanks.

04:57.990 --> 05:00.370
We made it to the Nationals thanks to you.

05:00.830 --> 05:02.170
Are you sure?

05:03.720 --> 05:07.190
Do you really think that?

05:10.170 --> 05:11.050
Yeah.

05:11.640 --> 05:12.780
Of course.

05:13.450 --> 05:13.450
Are you still at school?

05:13.450 --> 05:14.710
Reina

05:13.450 --> 05:14.710
Reina

05:13.450 --> 05:14.710
I just finished practice.
 Where are you now?

05:14.750 --> 05:17.250
Reina

05:14.750 --> 05:17.250
Reina

05:14.750 --> 05:17.250
I just finished practice.
 Where are you now?

05:14.750 --> 05:17.250
Are you still at school?

05:14.750 --> 05:17.250
Yeah, I'm about to go to the staff office.
 Wanna wait for me?

05:17.250 --> 05:18.290
Are you still at school?

05:17.250 --> 05:18.290
Yeah, I'm about to go to the staff office.
 Wanna wait for me?

05:17.250 --> 05:18.290
No, it's fine.

05:17.250 --> 05:18.290
Reina

05:17.250 --> 05:18.290
Reina

05:19.260 --> 05:20.740
Good work.

05:21.290 --> 05:23.280
Get home safe.

05:23.280 --> 05:23.970
Okay.

05:24.970 --> 05:27.710
<i>"I'm glad we made it to the Nationals,"</i>

05:28.110 --> 05:30.780
<i>is something that part 
of me just wouldn't let me say.</i>

05:31.660 --> 05:33.090
Pardon me.

05:34.230 --> 05:35.400
Oumae-san.

05:36.610 --> 05:37.540
Yes?

05:37.540 --> 05:41.440
Your speech before the concert 
was exemplary of a president.

05:41.440 --> 05:45.320
I just said what I was thinking, though.

05:45.320 --> 05:51.300
I have a habit of being 
cold in those situations.

05:51.700 --> 05:55.050
I even got in trouble for it during college.

05:55.530 --> 05:56.740
Never mind.

05:56.740 --> 05:58.720
I shouldn't talk about that now.

05:59.580 --> 06:02.580
Do you think she's happy for you?

06:02.580 --> 06:03.630
Yes.

06:03.630 --> 06:08.300
But she would say it was 
the students' hard work.

06:08.720 --> 06:09.930
Do you think so?

06:10.850 --> 06:13.770
It's been two years since 
I started teaching here.

06:14.220 --> 06:18.520
To be honest, I wasn't sure 
I could stay motivated.

06:19.090 --> 06:22.610
I'm practically performing with a 
band that has new members every year,

06:22.610 --> 06:25.390
working towards a competition 
that happens only once a year.

06:25.390 --> 06:26.780
That's true.

06:26.780 --> 06:32.420
Now that you mention it, school concert 
bands are weird, aren't they?

06:32.960 --> 06:37.420
There's something I said to 
her when we were in college.

06:37.420 --> 06:42.420
"It's as futile and thankless as 
stacking rocks on the River Styx."

06:43.840 --> 06:47.170
How did your wife respond?

06:50.880 --> 06:52.260
That they aren't rocks.

06:52.860 --> 06:55.080
They're people.

07:04.160 --> 07:07.830
Congratulations, Midori-chan!

07:04.160 --> 07:07.830
Congratulations, Kawashima-san.

07:07.830 --> 07:09.690
Thank you!

07:09.690 --> 07:12.530
Lucky, you got in on recommendation?

07:12.530 --> 07:16.580
I'm going straight into exam 
prep mode after the Nationals.

07:16.580 --> 07:19.970
I haven't even decided what 
I'm doing after high school.

07:20.920 --> 07:22.450
You haven't?!

07:24.050 --> 07:25.280
I mean...

07:25.960 --> 07:28.900
You're going to America, 
right, Reina-chan?

07:29.860 --> 07:31.300
America?!

07:32.360 --> 07:33.840
To study abroad?

07:34.980 --> 07:37.780
You hadn't told them?

07:37.780 --> 07:40.460
It's not confirmed yet.

07:40.460 --> 07:41.870
Where did you even hear about that?

07:41.870 --> 07:46.330
I overheard the teachers talking 
about it in the staff office.

07:46.330 --> 07:47.410
I'm sorry.

07:47.410 --> 07:49.360
No, it's fine, just...

07:49.950 --> 07:52.110
Will you be going alone?

07:52.110 --> 07:53.430
Aren't you worried?

07:53.430 --> 07:57.320
I'd be excited to go somewhere 
I've never been before.

07:57.320 --> 07:58.890
Ever the optimist.

08:00.640 --> 08:02.820
I tend to think...

08:02.820 --> 08:06.430
What we're doing right now is sowing seeds.

08:07.130 --> 08:14.740
We're planting the seeds for our unknown 
futures in all kinds of places.

08:20.220 --> 08:21.830
Here you are.

08:21.830 --> 08:23.100
Here we go!

08:23.100 --> 08:24.510
Should I cut it into quarters?

08:24.510 --> 08:25.940
That'd make them huge.

08:26.350 --> 08:28.280
It's more fun that way.

08:28.280 --> 08:29.750
It's massive.

08:29.750 --> 08:31.070
I like it, though.

08:31.070 --> 08:31.810
Yeah.

08:33.910 --> 08:36.250
I'm stuffed.

08:36.250 --> 08:37.230
Kumiko...

08:38.440 --> 08:41.420
I was going to tell you 
first once I knew for sure.

08:42.570 --> 08:44.570
Uh-huh.

08:44.570 --> 08:46.710
I'm more worried about you.

08:46.710 --> 08:48.780
What are you going to do, really?

08:48.780 --> 08:52.580
You don't need to change the subject.

08:52.930 --> 08:55.110
I'm not.

08:55.110 --> 08:56.920
It's September already.

08:59.540 --> 09:00.680
Wanna go?

09:01.710 --> 09:02.730
Isn't this...

09:02.730 --> 09:05.340
Yoroizuka-senpai's university?

09:02.730 --> 09:05.350
Regular Concert Series

09:05.700 --> 09:07.420
They're performing next week.

09:07.420 --> 09:09.100
Our senpais are going, too.

09:10.470 --> 09:11.870
Sure.

09:11.870 --> 09:13.270
If I'm just going.

09:15.030 --> 09:17.360
Do you still not want to go to music school?

09:31.420 --> 09:32.520
Kumiko...

09:33.200 --> 09:34.770
I know it's too late...

09:35.630 --> 09:37.880
But I shouldn't have said that 
you're a failure of a president.

09:38.290 --> 09:39.290
Also...

09:39.840 --> 09:45.520
I'm embarrassed I pushed you away and 
accused you of not doing anything.

09:46.820 --> 09:47.650
Sorry.

09:49.290 --> 09:50.860
No kidding!

09:50.860 --> 09:53.270
Your president's doing the 
best she can, you know!

09:55.780 --> 09:56.950
I know.

09:56.950 --> 10:00.740
But I'm where I am now 
because you're so selfish.

10:05.510 --> 10:07.240
Hug me to show me you love me.

10:07.240 --> 10:08.580
What?!

10:29.450 --> 10:34.860
<i>And so, before we could even revel in 
our victory in the Kansai Competition,</i>

10:35.390 --> 10:39.610
<i>we were right back to our grueling practice 
in pursuit of the national gold.</i>

10:40.120 --> 10:41.360
Okay.

10:41.920 --> 10:46.350
Now, please work on your issues 
in your individual sections.

10:46.350 --> 10:47.110
Yes.

10:47.580 --> 10:51.030
Also, about the auditions 
for the Nationals...

10:51.030 --> 10:53.330
They'll take place on Sunday 
two weeks from now.

10:56.450 --> 10:58.480
Please take the soli.

10:56.460 --> 10:58.470
Breathe with Reina

11:00.350 --> 11:04.480
I want Kumiko-senpai to play the soli part.

11:18.670 --> 11:20.120
<i>I want to get good.</i>

11:20.690 --> 11:22.840
<i>That's what was on my mind as I played.</i>

11:24.050 --> 11:28.300
<i>I'll get so deep into it that I cry 
in frustration like Reina does.</i>

11:29.010 --> 11:31.130
<i>That's what was on my mind as I played.</i>

11:32.450 --> 11:36.190
<i>Reina still hasn't changed.</i>

11:36.190 --> 11:37.740
<i>She's just as she's always been.</i>

11:39.020 --> 11:40.970
<i>She's completely unwavering.</i>

11:41.460 --> 11:43.570
<i>Just as earnest as she was that day.</i>

11:45.030 --> 11:47.800
<i>Yet I...</i>

11:52.970 --> 11:54.150
Mayu-chan.

11:57.840 --> 11:59.160
What's up?

12:07.250 --> 12:11.860
I'm going to forfeit the soli.

12:13.750 --> 12:14.880
Why?

12:15.410 --> 12:17.140
The same reason I've always told you.

12:17.140 --> 12:19.490
It's better for the club that way.

12:20.730 --> 12:25.550
You were chosen for the soli because 
of the work you put into it.

12:26.230 --> 12:28.420
Do you really want to let it go so casually?

12:28.640 --> 12:29.850
Yes. I don't care.

12:32.780 --> 12:37.950
I don't like seeing people 
suffer or being miserable.

12:38.940 --> 12:41.020
I said I'm not miserable—

12:41.020 --> 12:43.350
I want to do this for you.

12:44.420 --> 12:46.360
I've told you over and over.

12:46.360 --> 12:47.190
I...

12:47.830 --> 12:50.940
You want to play the soli with 
Kousaka-san one last time.

12:51.540 --> 12:53.460
Isn't that what you really want?

12:57.500 --> 13:02.240
What I really want is to compete 
fairly in the audition.

13:02.750 --> 13:06.550
I worked hard for three years 
believing that that's correct.

13:11.490 --> 13:13.400
That's not what you really want.

13:15.780 --> 13:17.210
It's not.

13:21.920 --> 13:24.240
You should ignore her.

13:26.350 --> 13:28.450
You shouldn't eavesdrop.

13:28.820 --> 13:32.010
You'll go crazy taking her seriously.

13:32.970 --> 13:37.130
Kuroe-senpai is insulting you.

13:37.870 --> 13:39.390
Can't you tell?

13:39.390 --> 13:40.720
That's a stretch.

13:40.720 --> 13:42.590
It isn't.

13:42.590 --> 13:44.570
You were listening, weren't you?

13:44.570 --> 13:48.460
Mayu-chan's not sure she should take it.

13:49.210 --> 13:51.630
Do you honestly think that?

13:52.650 --> 13:53.750
Yeah.

13:53.750 --> 13:55.110
I know how she feels.

13:59.150 --> 14:01.090
Then let me ask you...

14:01.090 --> 14:05.770
If you were in her position, 
would you bother discussing it?

14:06.330 --> 14:08.860
Over and over?

14:09.160 --> 14:12.390
Would you say the same 
thing to the other person?

14:12.390 --> 14:17.350
She'd never come to talk to you if she 
were really intent on forfeiting.

14:18.890 --> 14:22.090
Just like I never did.

14:22.570 --> 14:23.940
Kanade-chan...

14:23.940 --> 14:27.340
Kuroe-senpai is talking to you on purpose.

14:27.760 --> 14:30.490
To make you tell her that 
you want her to forfeit.

14:30.490 --> 14:34.500
That you want the soli part.

14:36.950 --> 14:39.780
<i>I felt a chill down my spine.</i>

14:42.470 --> 14:46.560
<i>Maybe there was part of me that 
was pretending not to see it.</i>

14:49.960 --> 14:51.710
And you wouldn't mind?

14:52.260 --> 14:55.080
I'd like to play euphonium if I do join.

14:55.560 --> 14:57.820
I want to have fun performing
with the others.

14:57.820 --> 15:00.500
I just want to play with everyone.

15:03.420 --> 15:05.200
<i>My selfish wants...</i>

15:06.580 --> 15:10.240
<i>Mayu-chan's selfish wants.</i>

15:14.100 --> 15:15.600
I see...

15:17.800 --> 15:18.770
See?

15:18.770 --> 15:22.470
There was nothing wrong with 
you playing, was there?

15:22.820 --> 15:24.130
I don't know.

15:24.740 --> 15:28.450
I thought it was fine that you played.

15:32.210 --> 15:34.880
You don't need to keep coming home.

15:34.880 --> 15:37.460
It's a classical concert, isn't it?

15:37.790 --> 15:40.340
You should dress up a little.

15:40.340 --> 15:42.360
You're just playing with me.

15:42.360 --> 15:44.060
I'm not.

15:44.060 --> 15:46.970
You should learn a little
 about this kind of thing.

15:46.970 --> 15:49.760
So, which college are you applying to again?

15:50.260 --> 15:52.280
I haven't decided yet.

15:52.280 --> 15:53.360
Ah.

15:55.330 --> 15:56.600
What about music school?

15:57.180 --> 15:59.780
Probably not music school.

15:59.780 --> 16:01.080
Why not?

16:01.700 --> 16:02.940
Just because.

16:03.360 --> 16:05.160
Guess I'm not changing your mind, then.

16:06.070 --> 16:07.480
Sit still.

16:07.950 --> 16:12.590
"Just because" is the 
hardest reason to argue with.

16:12.590 --> 16:14.240
Was it the same for you?

16:14.650 --> 16:15.800
Basically.

16:17.430 --> 16:18.910
So at school...

16:20.540 --> 16:25.740
We had an audition, and another 
girl ended up with my soli part.

16:28.680 --> 16:34.050
I plan to get really good and take it back.

16:34.730 --> 16:37.570
But, I don't know...

16:38.420 --> 16:40.490
There. You look cute.

16:40.490 --> 16:44.870
Now you just need some lip 
gloss, and you're done.

16:46.890 --> 16:50.310
I guess that's what it 
means to grow up, huh?

16:50.310 --> 16:51.010
Huh?

16:51.560 --> 16:52.950
Not that I'd know.

16:55.760 --> 16:57.850
See? You're cute.

16:59.280 --> 17:02.080
What's with the dress? Are you 
a pretentious middle schooler?

17:02.080 --> 17:04.340
You're a fourth-grader.

17:04.340 --> 17:06.550
How does this make me a fourth-grader?!

17:06.550 --> 17:07.770
Chill.

17:07.270 --> 17:08.950
Long time.

17:10.650 --> 17:12.460
It's been a really long time!

17:12.460 --> 17:14.510
What were you arguing about?

17:14.510 --> 17:17.220
Not arguing. Just roasting her.

17:17.220 --> 17:20.570
What? Don't you mean you 
were getting roasted?

17:22.060 --> 17:26.240
They have a band together, but their 
priorities are polar opposites of each other.

17:26.240 --> 17:28.820
And yet they're playing together, huh?

17:28.820 --> 17:30.640
They're besties.

17:30.640 --> 17:31.600
What are you, a kid?

17:31.860 --> 17:32.780
Let's go.

17:32.780 --> 17:33.680
Okay.

17:33.680 --> 17:35.860
Let's go, dummies.

17:34.420 --> 17:35.680
It's so nice.

17:35.680 --> 17:36.570
Yeah.

17:35.860 --> 17:37.470
Don't call me a dummy!

17:37.470 --> 17:39.340
Is Mizore up soon?

17:37.470 --> 17:41.220
To retain that kind of a
relationship even after graduating.

17:39.700 --> 17:40.830
Have you heard?

17:40.830 --> 17:42.830
Yeah. It should be pretty soon.

17:43.970 --> 17:44.970
Let's go.

17:44.970 --> 17:45.750
Okay.

18:34.260 --> 18:37.540
Yoroizuka-senpai's already playing solos.

18:37.540 --> 18:38.590
Yeah.

18:38.590 --> 18:39.920
She was amazing.

18:43.540 --> 18:53.860
<i>Reina must have been picturing herself 
playing at greater heights, like Yoroizuka-senpai.</i>

18:48.630 --> 18:51.250
Mizore looked so confident.

18:52.070 --> 18:54.790
I got nostalgic.

18:54.790 --> 18:56.380
Oh, there she is.

19:01.140 --> 19:02.740
Mizore!

19:02.740 --> 19:04.610
Over here!

19:07.390 --> 19:08.540
Guys.

19:10.610 --> 19:12.160
Calm down.

19:15.230 --> 19:17.720
Thanks for coming, everyone.

19:17.720 --> 19:19.630
Yeah, it was really good.

19:19.630 --> 19:22.140
The solo was moving.

19:22.140 --> 19:24.910
Thanks for coming, you two.

19:24.910 --> 19:27.520
No, I learned a lot.

19:27.910 --> 19:28.960
I see.

19:28.960 --> 19:32.050
Kousaka's going to a music school in America.

19:32.050 --> 19:33.020
America?

19:33.290 --> 19:34.270
Yes.

19:34.270 --> 19:37.640
I'm glad I got to hear this 
university in person.

19:39.200 --> 19:40.150
Good luck.

19:40.440 --> 19:42.870
By the way, where are you going, Oumae-chan?

19:44.130 --> 19:47.400
Actually, I haven't made up my mind yet.

19:47.400 --> 19:48.250
Seriously?!

19:48.250 --> 19:50.010
It's almost October!

19:50.010 --> 19:51.270
I know...

19:51.270 --> 19:54.690
Could you be considering 
Mizore's music school?

19:54.690 --> 19:58.740
No, well, music school...

19:58.740 --> 19:59.850
You aren't going, are you?

20:07.110 --> 20:08.890
Yoroizuka-senpai...

20:08.890 --> 20:14.860
What would you think if I ended 
up in your college next year?

20:17.300 --> 20:19.110
I wouldn't think anything.

20:20.560 --> 20:21.600
You wouldn't?

20:21.600 --> 20:25.620
I mean, I can't even picture you here.

20:38.490 --> 20:39.780
You're right.

20:43.310 --> 20:46.070
We have practice again tomorrow...

20:46.070 --> 20:49.010
Though that's over in a month, too.

20:49.720 --> 20:50.900
Oh, yeah.

20:51.420 --> 20:52.920
One more month.

20:59.330 --> 21:00.660
Reina!

21:01.080 --> 21:02.320
The signal's changing!

21:07.370 --> 21:08.390
See you.

21:08.390 --> 21:10.520
See you here in nine hours.

21:14.030 --> 21:14.750
Reina.

21:16.710 --> 21:20.750
I'm not going to music school.

21:22.720 --> 21:24.010
I see.

21:24.010 --> 21:25.270
All right.

21:27.250 --> 21:30.430
I'm ending things with you after this, then.

21:30.430 --> 21:31.510
Wha?

21:31.810 --> 21:33.440
I told you, remember?

21:33.440 --> 21:38.880
Once we don't have our music in common, 
we'll gradually stop contacting each other.

21:40.320 --> 21:42.860
We'll end up further away from each other.

21:44.960 --> 21:46.020
Reina...

21:46.020 --> 21:49.370
I don't want to end up like that with you.

21:49.370 --> 21:55.050
So I might as well end it now 
and hold on to what we have.

22:01.650 --> 22:03.120
Of course you'd say that.

22:03.950 --> 22:05.550
Please don't laugh.

22:12.380 --> 22:13.620
It'll be fine.

22:14.020 --> 22:15.860
We won't change.

22:16.920 --> 22:17.990
Kumiko...

22:19.280 --> 22:21.210
You're special, after all.

22:22.600 --> 22:25.630
You're never going to change for me.

22:25.630 --> 22:27.440
You're my special person.

22:30.930 --> 22:31.880
Okay...

22:34.450 --> 22:36.940
I'll go and become even more special.

22:36.940 --> 22:37.740
Yeah.

23:08.320 --> 23:09.700
<b>Music Room</b>

23:09.920 --> 23:12.930
All right, let's begin the auditions.

23:17.330 --> 23:23.210
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

23:22.000 --> 23:25.960
<b>To be continued</b>
